+# Browser Express Crash Backend API
+
+Last updated: 2026-06-01
+
+This document defines the backend work required to receive, store, symbolicate,
+and triage Browser Express Android crash reports.
+
+The current app implementation can use the existing Browser Express backend
+domain. A new standalone server is not required, but the crash ingestion
+surface must be isolated from normal product APIs because it accepts anonymous
+uploads and stores sensitive crash artifacts.
+
+## Goals
+
+* Receive native minidumps from the Browser Express Android Chromium fork.
+* Receive privacy-safe JSON crash events from the Android app.
+* Receive release symbol archives from CI through an authenticated endpoint.
+* Return responses compatible with Chromium's minidump uploader.
+* Store raw crash artifacts durably for later processing.
+* Symbolicate crashes using the matching release symbols.
+* Preserve user privacy and avoid collecting stable user identifiers.
+* Provide enough metadata for crash grouping, dashboards, and support triage.
+
+## Non-Goals
+
+* Do not require user login for app crash uploads.
+* Do not store page URLs, page titles, account identifiers, email addresses,
+  advertising IDs, Android IDs, or custom device identifiers.
+* Do not reuse Brave or Google crash ingestion endpoints.
+* Do not process minidumps synchronously in the upload request.
+
+## Recommended Deployment
+
+Use the existing backend infrastructure, but implement a dedicated crash module:
+
+```text
+api.browser.express
+  /crash/android/upload     public app crash ingestion
+  /crash/android/symbols    private CI symbol upload
+  /crash/health             health check
+```
+
+Recommended internal components:
+
+```text
+App upload endpoint
+  -> validate request
+  -> create report id
+  -> write raw artifact to object storage
+  -> write metadata row
+  -> enqueue symbolication or indexing job
+  -> return 2xx quickly
+
+Symbol upload endpoint
+  -> authenticate CI token
+  -> validate archive metadata
+  -> write symbol archive to object storage
+  -> write symbol metadata row
+  -> enqueue symbol unpack/index job
+```
+
+The upload endpoint should live behind HTTPS, a load balancer, request-size
+limits, and rate limiting. It should not share controller logic with normal
+authenticated API routes.
+
+## App Configuration
+
+Official Android builds must set:
+
+```gn
+browser_express_crash_upload_url = "https://api.browser.express/crash/android/upload"
+browser_express_crash_product = "BrowserExpress_Android"
+```
+
+The app appends query parameters to this configured URL:
+
+```text
+product=BrowserExpress_Android
+version=<app version>
+guid=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
+```
+
+For JSON events, the app also appends:
+
+```text
+report_type=browser_express_event
+```
+
+The zero GUID is intentional. Treat any non-zero `guid` as invalid, or store it
+as `null` and raise an internal alert.
+
+## Endpoint: App Upload
+
+### URL
+
+```http
+POST /crash/android/upload
+```
+
+This endpoint must accept two request types:
+
+* gzip-compressed multipart minidump uploads
+* JSON Browser Express event uploads
+
+Route by `Content-Type` and/or `report_type=browser_express_event`.
+
+### Common Query Parameters
+
+| Name | Required | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `product` | yes | Expected value: `BrowserExpress_Android`. |
+| `version` | yes | Browser Express app version from the build. |
+| `guid` | yes | Expected zero GUID only. Do not use as a user id. |
+| `report_type` | JSON only | `browser_express_event` for JSON event uploads. |
+
+Reject unknown products in production. Accept missing or unknown versions only
+with an explicit `unknown` bucket so ingestion does not break after a release.
+
+### Response Codes
+
+For minidumps, Chromium treats only these response codes as upload success:
+
+* `200 OK`
+* `201 Created`
+* `202 Accepted`
+
+The response body must be a plain text crash report id, for example:
+
+```text
+bex_01jz1y4x90m6t2ck8qcpb9sk2p
+```
+
+For JSON events, the app treats these response codes as success:
+
+* `200 OK`
+* `201 Created`
+* `202 Accepted`
+* `204 No Content`
+
+Prefer returning `202 Accepted` with a report id in the response body for both
+types.
+
+### Error Semantics
+
+Use:
+
+* `400` for malformed requests.
+* `401` or `403` only for private routes, not app crash uploads.
+* `413` for request body too large.
+* `415` for unsupported media type.
+* `429` for rate limiting.
+* `500` or `503` for temporary backend failures.
+
+The Android client retries failed minidump and JSON event uploads through its
+existing jobs. Avoid returning permanent 4xx unless the payload is truly
+unusable.
+
+## Minidump Upload Contract
+
+### Request
+
+The Android minidump uploader sends:
+
+```http
+POST /crash/android/upload?product=BrowserExpress_Android&version=0.0.276&guid=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
+Content-Encoding: gzip
+Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=<boundary>
+Connection: Keep-Alive
+```
+
+The request body is gzip-compressed multipart form data. Backend must:
+
+1. Detect `Content-Encoding: gzip`.
+2. Stream-decompress the body.
+3. Parse multipart using the `boundary` value.
+4. Find and store the minidump file part.
+5. Store bounded text metadata parts as report metadata.
+6. Return a crash report id immediately after durable write or queueing.
+
+Do not assume every multipart field name is stable. Chromium and Crashpad may
+include fields such as product, version, process type, platform metadata,
+upload file names, crash keys, and minidump file parts. Store unknown text
+fields only if they pass privacy filtering and size limits.
+
+### Size Limits
+
+Recommended defaults:
+
+* compressed request body: 20 MB
+* decompressed multipart body: 80 MB
+* individual text field: 8 KB
+* total text metadata: 64 KB
+* minidump file part: 64 MB
+
+Reject larger uploads with `413`.
+
+### Minidump Storage
+
+Object storage path recommendation:
+
+```text
+crash/raw/android/minidump/yyyy/mm/dd/<report_id>/request.multipart.gz
+crash/raw/android/minidump/yyyy/mm/dd/<report_id>/minidump.dmp
+crash/raw/android/minidump/yyyy/mm/dd/<report_id>/metadata.json
+```
+
+The raw compressed request is useful for parser fixes, but it is sensitive.
+Restrict access and apply retention.
+
+## JSON Event Upload Contract
+
+### Request
+
+The Android JSON event uploader sends:
+
+```http
+POST /crash/android/upload?product=BrowserExpress_Android&version=0.0.276&guid=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&report_type=browser_express_event
+Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
+Connection: Keep-Alive
+```
+
+Maximum app-side file size is 16 KB. Backend should reject JSON bodies above
+32 KB.
+
+### Common Body Fields
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": 1,
+  "type": "browser_express_event",
+  "event_type": "non_fatal",
+  "product": "BrowserExpress_Android",
+  "version": "0.0.276",
+  "upload_transport": "browser_express_json",
+  "privacy": "no_url_no_title_no_account_no_device_id"
+}
+```
+
+Validate that:
+
+* `schema` is `1`.
+* `type` is `browser_express_event`.
+* `product` matches query parameter `product`.
+* `version` matches query parameter `version`, or record mismatch as an
+  ingestion warning.
+* `privacy` is `no_url_no_title_no_account_no_device_id`.
+
+### Event Type: `android_exit`
+
+Body fields:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": 1,
+  "type": "browser_express_event",
+  "event_type": "android_exit",
+  "product": "BrowserExpress_Android",
+  "version": "0.0.276",
+  "upload_transport": "browser_express_json",
+  "privacy": "no_url_no_title_no_account_no_device_id",
+  "reason": "native",
+  "process_role": "browser",
+  "importance": "fg",
+  "age": "m",
+  "previous_session": {
+    "schema": 1,
+    "event_count": 4,
+    "events": ["app_create", "fg", "yt_pip_trigger", "yt_pip_error"],
+    "last_seen_age": "s"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Allowed `reason` values:
+
+```text
+anr, java, native, dep, resource, self, init, low_mem, perm, signal,
+user_req, user_stop, freezer, pkg_state, pkg_update, other, unknown
+```
+
+Allowed `process_role` values:
+
+```text
+browser, child, other
+```
+
+Allowed `importance` values:
+
+```text
+fg, fgs, vis, per, bg, cache
+```
+
+Allowed `age` values:
+
+```text
+na, s, m, h, d
+```
+
+Optional `previous_session` object:
+
+* May be omitted when the app has no previous-session journal.
+* `schema` must be `1`.
+* `event_count` must equal the number of entries in `events`.
+* `events` must contain at most 32 tokens, each matching
+  `^[a-z0-9_]{1,24}$`.
+* `last_seen_age` must be one of `na`, `s`, `m`, `h`, or `d`.
+* Reject URLs, page titles, account identifiers, device identifiers, raw
+  exception text, stack text, free-form strings, and values containing `/`,
+  `.`, `:`, `@`, spaces, or uppercase letters.
+
+### Event Type: `non_fatal`
+
+Body fields:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema": 1,
+  "type": "browser_express_event",
+  "event_type": "non_fatal",
+  "product": "BrowserExpress_Android",
+  "version": "0.0.276",
+  "upload_transport": "browser_express_json",
+  "privacy": "no_url_no_title_no_account_no_device_id",
+  "component": "youtube",
+  "code": "pip_restore_missing",
+  "severity": "warning"
+}
+```
+
+Token validation:
+
+* `component`, `code`, and `severity` must match `^[a-z0-9_]{1,32}$`.
+* Reject raw exception strings.
+* Reject values containing `/`, `.`, `:`, `@`, spaces, or uppercase letters.
+
+Known initial components:
+
+```text
+youtube, component
+```
+
+Known initial severities:
+
+```text
+info, warning, error
+```
+
+Known initial YouTube codes:
+
+```text
+pip_bottom_no_tab
+pip_bottom_unavailable
+pip_back_no_tab
+pip_back_unavailable
+pip_no_activity
+pip_intro_no_activity
+full_top_no_tab
+full_top_unavailable
+full_os_disabled
+pip_origin_missing
+pip_restore_missing
+pip_mode_change_error
+```
+
+### JSON Event Storage
+
+Object storage path recommendation:
+
+```text
+crash/raw/android/event/yyyy/mm/dd/<event_id>/event.json
+```
+
+JSON events are already privacy-safe enum payloads. They should still pass the
+same forbidden-key scanner before storage.
+
+## Endpoint: Symbol Upload
+
+### URL
+
+```http
+POST /crash/android/symbols
+Authorization: Bearer <ci-token>
+Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=<boundary>
+```
+
+This endpoint is called by CI/release tooling, not by the app.
+
+### Fields
+
+| Name | Required | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `product` | yes | `BrowserExpress_Android`. |
+| `version` | yes | Release version matching app uploads. |
+| `channel` | yes | `release`, `beta`, `nightly`, or `debug`. |
+| `symbols` | yes | Android symbol archive file. |
+
+The helper script sends the file field as `symbols`.
+
+### Authentication
+
+Use a secret token stored in CI:
+
+```text
+BROWSER_EXPRESS_SYMBOL_UPLOAD_TOKEN
+```
+
+Recommended backend behavior:
+
+* require HTTPS
+* require bearer token
+* support token rotation
+* audit every upload
+* limit upload size by channel and product
+* reject duplicate version/channel unless a privileged overwrite flag is used
+
+### Symbol Storage
+
+Object storage path recommendation:
+
+```text
+crash/symbols/android/<product>/<version>/<channel>/<upload_id>/symbols.tar
+crash/symbols/android/<product>/<version>/<channel>/<upload_id>/manifest.json
+```
+
+Store:
+
+* product
+* version
+* channel
+* archive checksum
+* archive size
+* upload time
+* CI build id if provided later
+* uploader principal
+
+After storage, enqueue an async symbol unpack/index job.
+
+## Database Model
+
+Suggested relational tables:
+
+### `crash_reports`
+
+| Column | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `id` | Server generated report id returned to app. |
+| `type` | `minidump` or `event`. |
+| `product` | `BrowserExpress_Android`. |
+| `version` | App version. |
+| `channel` | Optional if derived later. |
+| `platform` | `android`. |
+| `report_type` | Query `report_type`, nullable for minidumps. |
+| `event_type` | JSON event type, nullable for minidumps. |
+| `storage_uri` | Raw artifact object storage URI. |
+| `metadata_uri` | Metadata object storage URI. |
+| `received_at` | Ingestion timestamp. |
+| `status` | `received`, `queued`, `symbolicated`, `failed`. |
+| `privacy_status` | `passed`, `rejected`, `scrubbed`. |
+
+### `crash_events`
+
+| Column | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `report_id` | FK to `crash_reports`. |
+| `event_type` | `android_exit` or `non_fatal`. |
+| `component` | Non-fatal component. |
+| `code` | Non-fatal code. |
+| `severity` | Non-fatal severity. |
+| `reason` | Android exit reason. |
+| `process_role` | `browser`, `child`, `other`. |
+| `importance` | Android importance bucket. |
+| `age` | Exit age bucket. |
+
+### `symbol_files`
+
+| Column | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `id` | Server generated symbol upload id. |
+| `product` | `BrowserExpress_Android`. |
+| `version` | Release version. |
+| `channel` | Release channel. |
+| `storage_uri` | Archive object URI. |
+| `sha256` | Archive checksum. |
+| `size_bytes` | Archive size. |
+| `uploaded_at` | Upload timestamp. |
+| `status` | `stored`, `indexed`, `failed`. |
+
+### `symbolication_jobs`
+
+| Column | Description |
+| --- | --- |
+| `id` | Job id. |
+| `report_id` | Crash report id. |
+| `symbol_file_id` | Matching symbol file if found. |
+| `status` | `queued`, `running`, `done`, `failed`, `missing_symbols`. |
+| `attempts` | Retry count. |
+| `last_error` | Bounded operational error text. |
+
+## Privacy Requirements
+
+Crash dumps can contain memory. Treat them as sensitive even when the app does
+not intentionally send personal data.
+
+Required controls:
+
+* no public read access to crash object storage
+* restricted admin access with audit logs
+* no raw crash body in application logs
+* no query string logging if it can include future identifiers
+* no stable user id storage
+* no full IP retention beyond abuse prevention needs
+* retention policy for raw minidumps
+* separate retention policy for aggregated crash stats
+
+Forbidden JSON keys and metadata keys:
+
+```text
+url
+uri
+href
+title
+email
+account
+account_id
+user
+user_id
+profile_id
+device_id
+android_id
+advertising_id
+gaid
+guid
+client_id
+cookie
+authorization
+token
+```
+
+For JSON events, reject if any forbidden key exists at any object depth, except
+the query parameter `guid` which must be the zero GUID and should not be stored
+as an identifier.
+
+For minidump multipart text fields, allowlist preferred fields and drop unknown
+fields unless explicitly approved.
+
+## Rate Limiting and Abuse Protection
+
+App crash uploads are anonymous. Use operational limits:
+
+* per-IP request rate limits
+* per-version request rate limits
+* global circuit breaker
+* body-size limits before decompression
+* decompressed-size limits during streaming
+* gzip bomb protection
+* multipart part-count limit
+* JSON parser depth limit
+* object storage write timeout
+
+Do not block normal users permanently based only on IP. Mobile networks and
+VPNs share IPs heavily.
+
+## Symbolication
+
+Minimum backend behavior:
+
+1. Store minidump.
+2. Find matching symbols by product, version, platform, and channel if present.
+3. Run symbolication async.
+4. Store symbolicated stack trace separately from raw dump.
+5. Mark crashes with missing symbols for release pipeline follow-up.
+
+The current release tooling can create Android symbol artifacts through the
+existing build targets and upload archives through:
+
+```sh
+BROWSER_EXPRESS_SYMBOL_UPLOAD_URL="https://api.browser.express/crash/android/symbols" \
+BROWSER_EXPRESS_SYMBOL_UPLOAD_TOKEN="<ci-token>" \
+python3 script/browser_express_upload_crash_symbols.py \
+  --symbols-archive ../out/android_Release_arm64/dist/Defaultarm64.tar \
+  --version 0.0.276 \
+  --channel release
+```
+
+Release CI should run the release gate before publishing:
+
+```sh
+python3 script/browser_express_crash_release_gate.py \
+  --out-dir ../out/android_Release_arm64 \
+  --require-official-config \
+  --require-symbols \
+  --check-tracking-doc
+```
+
+## Triage Features
+
+Backend/dashboard should provide:
+
+* crash count by version and day
+* crash-free sessions later when session counts exist
+* top crash groups by version
+* top non-fatal event codes
+* Android exit reasons by version
+* missing-symbols queue
+* first seen and last seen per crash group
+* regression detection between releases
+* exportable report id for customer support
+
+Crash grouping suggestion:
+
+```text
+group_key = sha256(product + version_major_minor + exception_type_or_signal
+                  + top_in_app_frame + process_type)
+```
+
+For JSON-only events:
+
+```text
+group_key = sha256(product + version + event_type + component + code + reason)
+```
+
+## Monitoring and Alerts
+
+Add alerts for:
+
+* upload endpoint 5xx rate
+* upload endpoint p95 latency
+* object storage write failures
+* queue depth
+* symbolication failures
+* missing symbols for an official version
+* forbidden privacy key rejection spikes
+* non-zero GUID uploads
+* crash volume spike after release
+
+## Retention
+
+Suggested defaults:
+
+* raw minidumps: 30 to 90 days
+* symbolicated stack traces: 180 to 365 days
+* aggregate crash counts: 2 years
+* raw JSON events: 90 days
+* aggregated JSON event counts: 1 year
+* symbol archives: keep for every supported released version
+
+Confirm retention with legal/privacy requirements before production launch.
+
+## Test Plan
+
+Backend developer should implement automated tests for:
+
+* valid gzip multipart minidump upload returns `202` and report id
+* minidump upload without gzip is rejected or handled explicitly
+* malformed multipart returns `400`
+* oversized compressed body returns `413`
+* gzip bomb protection returns `413`
+* valid JSON `android_exit` event returns success
+* valid JSON `android_exit` event with `previous_session` returns success
+* valid JSON `non_fatal` event returns success
+* JSON with forbidden key `url` is rejected
+* JSON with non-zero `guid` query param is rejected or flagged
+* symbol upload without token returns `401`
+* symbol upload with token stores archive and metadata
+* duplicate symbol upload policy is enforced
+* object storage failure returns retryable `503`
+
+Manual JSON event smoke test:
+
+```sh
+curl -i \
+  -X POST \
+  "https://api.browser.express/crash/android/upload?product=BrowserExpress_Android&version=0.0.276&guid=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&report_type=browser_express_event" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8" \
+  --data '{"schema":1,"type":"browser_express_event","event_type":"non_fatal","product":"BrowserExpress_Android","version":"0.0.276","upload_transport":"browser_express_json","privacy":"no_url_no_title_no_account_no_device_id","component":"youtube","code":"pip_restore_missing","severity":"warning"}'
+```
+
+Expected response:
+
+```http
+HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted
+Content-Type: text/plain
+
+bex_<server_generated_id>
+```
+
+## Production Readiness Checklist
+
+Before setting `browser_express_crash_upload_url` in an official build:
+
+* HTTPS endpoint deployed.
+* Minidump upload path tested with gzip multipart.
+* JSON event path tested.
+* Object storage bucket private and encrypted.
+* Database tables migrated.
+* Async queue deployed.
+* Symbol upload endpoint deployed with CI token.
+* Symbolication worker deployed.
+* Dashboard or query access available to engineering.
+* Alerts configured.
+* Retention configured.
+* Access audit logging enabled.
+* Release CI runs crash release gate.
+* Release CI uploads symbols before rollout.
